menu "LBR CAN bus"

    config LBR_CAN_TX_GPIO
        int "TWAI TX GPIO (to transceiver TXD)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            GPIO driving the CAN transceiver TXD pin. -1 means not configured:
            pins are TBD until the node schematic is confirmed (issue #15),
            and the node refuses to start CAN while this is -1.

    config LBR_CAN_RX_GPIO
        int "TWAI RX GPIO (from transceiver RXD)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            GPIO reading the CAN transceiver RXD pin. -1 means not configured.

    config LBR_CAN_BITRATE
        int "CAN bit rate (bit/s)"
        default 1000000
        help
            Shared bus bit rate; every node must use the same value. The
            1 Mbit/s default suits a vehicle-length harness (well under the
            ~40 m limit) and is provisional until harness length, stub
            lengths, and topology are confirmed (issue #15). The system CAN
            budget in docs/can-ids.md is computed at this rate.

    config LBR_CAN_RX_QUEUE_LEN
        int "RX queue length (frames)"
        default 256

    config LBR_CAN_TX_QUEUE_LEN
        int "TX queue length (frames)"
        default 64
        help
            Must hold a node's worst-case burst: every slot and the 12
            heartbeat pages can come due at the same instant (checked for
            every plan in dev/tests/host/test_plans.c).

    config LBR_CAN_NODE_BUDGET_PERMILLE
        int "Per-node CAN bandwidth budget (permille of bit rate)"
        range 10 800
        default 150
        help
            A node configuration whose worst-case CAN load exceeds this share
            of the bus is rejected at boot. The system-wide plan lives in
            docs/can-ids.md.

endmenu
